b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 689.0 Td (================================================================================) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 675.5 Td () Tj
b'/F2 9.5 Tf' 40 662.0 Td (Q.1 \(a\) Explain RSA Algorithm. Given prime numbers p = 7, q = 11, and public exponent) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 648.5 Td (     e = 13:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 635.0 Td (\(i\) Calculate modulus n and Euler totient phi\(n\).) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 621.5 Td (\(ii\) Compute private key d.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 608.0 Td (\(iii\) Encrypt plaintext M = 9 and decrypt the resulting ciphertext. [10 Marks]) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 594.5 Td (Answer:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 581.0 Td (Step 1: Compute n and phi\(n\):) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 567.5 Td (n = p  q = 7  11 = 77.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 554.0 Td (phi\(n\) = \(p - 1\)  \(q - 1\) = \(7 - 1\)  \(11 - 1\) = 6  10 = 60.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 540.5 Td () Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 527.0 Td (Step 2: Calculate private key d:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 513.5 Td (d  e = 1 \(mod phi\(n\)\) => 13  d = 1 \(mod 60\).) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 500.0 Td (Using Extended Euclidean Algorithm:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 486.5 Td (13  37 = 481 = \(8  60\) + 1 = 1 \(mod 60\).) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 473.0 Td (Hence, private key d = 37.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 459.5 Td () Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 446.0 Td (Step 3: Encryption of M = 9:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 432.5 Td (Ciphertext C = M^e mod n = 9^13 mod 77.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 419.0 Td (9^2 = 81 = 4 \(mod 77\)) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 405.5 Td (9^4 = 4^2 = 16 \(mod 77\)) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 392.0 Td (9^8 = 16^2 = 256 = 25 \(mod 77\)) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 378.5 Td (9^13 = 9^8  9^4  9^1 = 25  16  9 \(mod 77\)) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 365.0 Td (25  16 = 400 = 15 \(mod 77\)) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 351.5 Td (15  9 = 135 = 58 \(mod 77\).) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 338.0 Td (Ciphertext C = 58.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 324.5 Td () Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 311.0 Td (Step 4: Decryption:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 297.5 Td (Plaintext M = C^d mod n = 58^37 mod 77 = 9. \(Successfully Decrypted!\)) Tj
